-- title:
--   Local box of a maximal order is a conjugate of M₂(ℤᵥ)
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order in the sense of the project: $\Lambda$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is the whole algebra and it is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, and every $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda'$ with these four properties and containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $v$ be a height one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, write $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion and $\mathcal{O}_v$ for its valuation subring, and let $\varphi\colon \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ be a ring isomorphism such that $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for every $r\in\mathbb{Q}_v$. Then there exists $h\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ such that for every $x$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$: $x$ lies in the local box of $\Lambda$ at $v$, that is, in the additive subgroup generated by the elementary tensors $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c\in\mathcal{O}_v$, if and only if all four entries of $h^{-1}\,\varphi(x)\,h$ lie in $\mathcal{O}_v$.
--
--   This is the local description of a maximal quaternion order at a place where the algebra splits: its local box is carried by $\varphi$ onto a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$-conjugate of $M_2(\mathcal{O}_v)$, so that all maximal orders are locally conjugate. It underlies the local computations with Eichler orders and their idelic stabilisers used in the Cerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where it is cited in the analysis of Hecke sets and of stabilisers of local boxes.
